{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Phase 2 complete — RED→GREEN fix + Step-7 sibling sweep.\n\nDETERMINISTIC REPRODUCTION (RED): `REBAR_HLC_NOW=1788072768731609343` forces the CREATE tick to the float64-exact 1788072768731609344; `test_export_timestamps_round_trip_exactly` then fails deterministically with the exact CI message. Post-fix: 0/60 fresh-process runs fail (fixture is now clock-independent; pre-fix Monte-Carlo rate ~0.399% ≈ 1/256).\n\nFIX (test-only, no product code): the `ns_ticket` fixture injects `REBAR_HLC_NOW` = a fixed multiple-of-256 base (`_HLC_INEXACT_BASE_NS`), so stored created_at=base+1 and updated_at=base+2 are DETERMINISTICALLY float64-inexact; a fixture precondition asserts inexactness, and a new `test_ns_ticket_timestamps_are_deterministically_float64_inexact` guard pins it. The lossless-string assertions are unchanged (not weakened). monkeypatch.setenv auto-reverts; it overrides any external clock, so the fix holds even under an adversarial `REBAR_HLC_NOW`.\n\nMUTATION CHECK (teeth, sandboxed): seeding the exact confirmed root cause (base → base-1, making created_at float64-exact) returns the target test AND the guard to deterministic RED on both files; restored after.\n\nSTEP 7 — CONSTRUCT SWEEP: swept tests/ for the `int(float(x)) != x` wall-clock-hazard construct. Confirmed ONE sibling: tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_js_safe_integers.py::test_show_timestamp_round_trips_exactly — identical class (its `ns_ticket` fixture stamps a wall-clock draw, then `assert int(float(stored)) != stored`), same ~1/256 flake. FIXED IN SCOPE under the same discipline (same deterministic-clock fixture fix + inexactness precondition; sandboxed mutation → RED confirmed). Non-siblings in that file (test_multi_ticket_json_surfaces_are_js_safe etc.) only assert `> JS_SAFE_MAX` / substring presence — not the fragile premise — so they are not flaky. No other construct hits in tests/.\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA (class scope):\n1. test_export_ndjson_js_safe.py::test_export_timestamps_round_trip_exactly is deterministic (no wall-clock data dependency). ✓\n2. test_cli_js_safe_integers.py::test_show_timestamp_round_trips_exactly is deterministic (sibling). ✓\n3. Both `ns_ticket` fixtures enforce float64-inexactness deterministically (precondition + guard test). ✓\n4. Lossless-string wire assertions unchanged. ✓\n\nSTEP 7 — PARITY SWEEP: N/A — the fixed artifact is a per-test fixture data assumption, not a multi-channel operation.\n\nVALIDATION: both modules GREEN (14 passed); `make lint` PASS; `make typecheck` Success (706 files). File impact recorded on both paths. Both files are test-only — outside eb64's domain (_store/ / reconciler / src/rebar/llm/), so no conflict."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788089111232974812,"uuid":"f85f33d0-fb34-4341-ac6f-9f56086fb5a5"}